      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "The restricted twist on N is trivial. The closed subgroup of N on which z vanishes is normal in G and contains the generating inertia groups. At the remaining places a nontrivial scalar on a cyclotomic generator yields a local primitive. Changing a prolongation transports that primitive by an explicit formula. Tower.desc applies resInfInj and resInfOnto to construct the equivalence used by INP-16.",
